  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 220C, fan-forced. Line an oven tray with baking paper. Cut the cauliflower into small florets. Cut the unpeeled pumpkin into 1cm-thick wedges, then halve widthwise (see Make it yours). Crush ½ garlic clove. Drain and rinse the chickpeas.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2472340/photos/large/prep_ingredients-505f9e6071819706469af2db661720f2.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast veggies: Combine the chermoula seasoning and 1 tbs olive oil in a large bowl and season with salt and pepper. Add the cauliflower and pumpkin and toss to coat. Put on the lined tray, reserving the bowl. Roast for 20 mins. Scatter the chickpeas over the veggies and roast for a further 10 mins or until the veggies are tender.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2472341/photos/large/roast_veggies-eb3f9dc70c1c2054ba050225ed6e1364.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Toast pistachios: Meanwhile, put the pistachios in a cold small frypan over medium heat. Cook, tossing, for 3-4 mins until toasted. Remove from the pan.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2472342/photos/large/make_dressing-fa53f10875b28c3de8a0735eec930c96.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make dressing: Put the yoghurt, garlic, 2 tsp white wine vinegar, ½ tsp honey and ¼ tsp chilli flakes, if using, in a bowl. Season with salt and pepper and whisk to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2472343/photos/large/toast_nuts-9eeed132030da05987d9097926cb6e07.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Coarsely chop the pistachios. Put the spinach and roast veggies and chickpeas in the reserved bowl. Season with salt and pepper and toss to combine. Divide the salad among bowls, drizzle with the dressing, scatter over the pistachios and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2472344/photos/large/serve_up-1f9517b07f8ddf9bbab40c4a97a4849e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: Pumpkin skin is edible, nutritious and delicious, especially when roasted. Leaving the skin on also saves time and waste, but you can remove it if you prefer.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2472345/photos/large/did_you_know-705b976187c4e8f1a33192958419dfb7.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
